WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.466 --> 00:00:03.633
[music]

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.800
[Instructor] So we have a lot
of our gameplay set up now,

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.233
so we can move around,
and dodge all these

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.133
enemy Obstacles coming our way.

5
00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:17.700
We can grab these Powerups.

6
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.933
Now, let's get started
from moving our project

7
00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:24.200
from a prototype to a bit
more complete project.

8
00:00:24.633 --> 00:00:28.200
To do that, we'll need to Import
our Assets that we're going to use.

9
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.700
Now, under this video you'll
find a link to download

10
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.566
the "Course Asset Library,"

11
00:00:32.566 --> 00:00:35.466
which you can download,
and Import into your project.

12
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.033
Once it's been Imported, you will find
the Course Library Folder

13
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:42.100
in your project window.
And now in our "Course Library,"

14
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.666
we can take a look at all
of the different options

15
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.666
that we have to use in our Project.
So for now, just go take a look at

16
00:00:49.666 --> 00:00:52.133
all of the different
Assets that you can use.

17
00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:00.900
And think about which ones
you're going to start using

18
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.933
to replace all of the different
things in your scene,

19
00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:08.800
like in my case, the walls, my player,
my prefabs and my Powerup,

20
00:01:09.233 --> 00:01:12.533
so that way it fits the design
of the game I was looking to create.

21
00:01:12.866 --> 00:01:15.666
So what you're going to do
is click on the link to download

22
00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:19.633
the Course Library Asset files,
and then Import them into your project,

23
00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.600
and then you can take
a look at that library

24
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.666
inside of the Project window
to find different Assets

25
00:01:25.666 --> 00:01:28.633
to replace with your player
and non-player Objects.

26
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:29.766
Now it's your turn.

27
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.066
[music]
